To elaborate: you can rustproof a piece of armor by confusing yourself, 
then reading either a *non-cursed* scroll of enchant armor OR a 
*cursed* scroll of destroy armor; a ?oEA will also repair existing 
damage when used this way, while a ?oDA will not. Unless you've been 
getting ?oEA aplenty all game and all of your final armor set's already 
well-enchanted, this is probably a waste of ?oEA. OTOH, fooproofing 
armor is one of only two good uses for a ?oDA that don't involve 
blanking it, the other being removing cursed junk armor.

Keep in mind, you can "rust"proof *any* piece of armor (cloak, helmet, 
shield, etc.), not just your suit; this will fireproof, rotproof, or 
corrodeproof things that cannot rust. Also, rustproofing mithril or 
dragon scale mail is a waste, as neither can be rusted, corroded, 
burned, or rotted.


